      "end_seconds": 6.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "I mean, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.96,
      "end_seconds": 15.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.33,
      "end_seconds": 25.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "um, it's a blocked nose for months i thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.01,
      "end_seconds": 33.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.05,
      "end_seconds": 36.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.78,
      "end_seconds": 41.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.0,
      "end_seconds": 67.39,
      "duration_seconds": 25.39,
      "text": "when it starts I tend to get a postnasal drip as well. I've been losing my sense of smell too, for about three months. Yeah, the postnasal drip? That's been for ten days. About postnasal drip, it's mild, honestly. I had a dull pressure over my face before. That's settled now, though"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 85.01,
      "end_seconds": 94.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "okay so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 79 BP is 119 over 74 SpO2 99 percent on room air temperature 36.4."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.32,
      "end_seconds": 97.02,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.58,
      "end_seconds": 103.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.12,
      "end_seconds": 106.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.55,
      "end_seconds": 125.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "there are pale, grape-like swellings inside both nostrils"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.74,
      "end_seconds": 136.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed. Let me check a few things. Any nosebleeds, fever or vision changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.25,
      "end_seconds": 143.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Sorry what was I saying no I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.56,
      "end_seconds": 151.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.16,
      "end_seconds": 154.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.9,
      "end_seconds": 161.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "right, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.37,
      "end_seconds": 167.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Yes, erythromycin, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.07,
      "end_seconds": 171.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.08,
      "end_seconds": 176.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "I have asthma i have eczema for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.39,
      "end_seconds": 183.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "okay, I can see eczema in your file as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.92,
      "end_seconds": 205.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.97,
      "end_seconds": 225.67,
      "duration_seconds": 18.7,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I work in accounts at a hospital. I swim twice a week. No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.66,
      "end_seconds": 241.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.08,
      "end_seconds": 246.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "oh no I've never been operated on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.5,
      "end_seconds": 255.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.44,
      "end_seconds": 271.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.25,
      "text": "I take Foracort inhaler twice a day for my asthma my neighbour said I should get it looked at so I'm on hydrocortisone cream when needed for the eczema"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.42,
      "end_seconds": 280.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "taking everything into account, this looks most like nasal polyps i'd also keep chronic sinusitis in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.5,
      "end_seconds": 283.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.38,
      "end_seconds": 308.12,
      "duration_seconds": 23.74,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's nasal polyps and we'll know more once the a nasal endoscopy is back. a nasal endoscopy is what I'd like next for nasal obstruction. What I'm giving you is mometasone nasal spray 50 micrograms two sprays each side once a day eight weeks. It's for nasal polyps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.14,
      "end_seconds": 310.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Thank you doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.87,
      "end_seconds": 329.86,
      "duration_seconds": 17.99,
      "text": "rinse with saline and use the spray daily. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. The ENT clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you. Let's plan a check in eight weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.9,
      "end_seconds": 333.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "right, I can manage that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.98,
      "end_seconds": 337.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.67,
      "end_seconds": 341.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "that's clear thanks"
    }
  ]
